  "limits": [
    "Local transition widths lie in (0, 0.5] of each source arc-length interval. Nonfinite, nonpositive, oversized or unrepresentable windows reject. Stored positive control increments qualify transition monotonicity; endpoint joins use quintic Hermite formulas. The final simple cubic basis supplies C2 fitted-curve and retained tensor continuity.",
    "All existing 1-to-32 source, 2-to-32 contact, degree-16 source, 128 input-control, 2048 total input-control, 125-span and 128 fitted-control limits remain. Native fitting uses its existing bounded parameter correction/geometric refitting and fresh sampled point measurements.",
    "Sampled fit distances are not continuous original-curve distance certificates or bounds on world-restoration rounding. Exact restored contact proofs and downstream continuous original-image certificates remain separate and unchanged. All twelve global/local regression originals and six local diagnostic originals pass at 1e-6.",
    "The local independent candidate improves the previous whole-interval diagnostic at the same degree/control count, but still fails the requested 1e-6 returned-point comparison. The earlier repeated-knot arc-length candidate remains slightly closer. No default or application command selects the local policy automatically.",
    "The retained reference audit separately proves one original query incompatible with simultaneous 1e-6 whole-source preservation and 1e-6 returned-point matching. This change does not relax either limit, enlarge proof work, hide that mismatch or qualify NetworkSrf interior fitting, topology, boundary continuity or performance.",
    "Release native test linkage uses AddressSanitizer and frame pointers in SMLib, SM_API and the adapter. Rust and the debug oracle are not separately instrumented. Leak and optional stack-use-after-return checks remain disabled. No new native C++ code changed in this milestone."
  ],
